@Wei

Well, the proposal is somewhat based on such ways to do. Unfortunately:

   - There's an issue about *WHO* is/are the "editor(s)" reviewing=20
   proposals.
   - The size of "core" Lojbanists is very small (as pointed out by=20
   Gregorio).
   - And we may not rely on a truly self-organizing community (as pointed=
=20
   out by Gleki) because of long history of internal "conflicts" & such.

So yes, the base idea is very interesting, but it seems it needs to be=20
adapted to the Lojban situation.


Le jeudi 23 novembre 2017 04:50:18 UTC+1, Wei Tang a =C3=A9crit :
>
> (Forgive me if I missed some comment above me. This thread is just too=20
> long.)
>
> Why don't we use an RFC-like process for improving Lojban? Putting=20
> everything in a central documentation CLL, IMHO, is not a good idea.
>
> We can have people freely submit new RFCs. Editor accepts them without=20
> subjective judgement (but only ensure that it is of good quality). New RF=
C=20
> starts with "Proposed" status, and once several Lojban text starts to use=
=20
> this derivative, it enters "Draft" status. If we have the majority of the=
=20
> community using it, the RFC becomes a "Standard".
>
> Reference: https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/rfc2026/
>

